{"Docs":[{"DocType":1,"IsAmended":false,"IsUpdated":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocOrderId":210,"AmendedBy":[],"Notes":[],"Drafts":[],"ChunkGroupStartingNodeId":"COCI_CH1GEPR","NodeDepth":2,"TitleHtml":"<div class=\"chunk-title\">Sec. 1-2. - Rules of construction and definitions.</div>","ShouldShowMiniToc":false,"Id":"COCI_CH1GEPR_S1-2RUCODE","Title":"Sec. 1-2. - Rules of construction and definitions.","Content":"<div class=\"chunk-content\">\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (a)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Generally.</span> In the construction of this Code and of all ordinances of the city, the rules and\n               definitions set out in this section shall apply and be observed, unless such construction\n               would be inconsistent with the manifest intent of the council, or unless the context\n               clearly requires otherwise.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (b)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">And, or.</span> The word \"and\" shall be read as \"or\" and the word \"or\" as \"and,\" where the sense\n               requires it.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (c)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Charter.</span> The word \"Charter\" shall mean the Norfolk Charter of 1918, as amended from time to\n               time.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (d)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">City.</span> The words \"city\", \"the city\" and \"this city\" shall be construed as if the words \"of\n               Norfolk, Virginia\" followed them.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (e)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Code.</span> Whenever the term \"Code\" or \"this Code\" is used without further qualification, it\n               shall mean the Code of the City of Norfolk, Virginia, 1979, as designated in <a href=\"\" data-chunk-id=\"COCI_CH1GEPR_S1-1HOCODECI\" class=\"section-link\" data-product-id=\"10121\">section 1-1</a>. Whenever reference is made to chapters or sections by number only, and without further\n               qualification, the reference shall apply to the appropriate chapter or section of\n               this Code.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (f)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Computation of time.</span> Whenever a notice is required to be given, or an act to be done, a certain length\n               of time before any proceeding shall be had, the day on which such notice is given,\n               or such act is done, shall be counted in computing the time, but the day on which\n               such proceeding is to be had shall not be counted.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (g)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Council.</span> Wherever the term \"council\" or \"city council\" is used, it shall be construed to mean\n               the council of the City of Norfolk, Virginia.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (h)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Gender.</span> A word importing the masculine gender only shall extend and be applied to females\n               and to firms, partnerships and corporations, as well as to males.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (i)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Number.</span> A word importing the singular number only may extend and be applied to several persons\n               or things as well as to one person or thing; and a word importing the plural number\n               only may extend and be applied to one person or thing, as well as to several persons\n               or things.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (j)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Oath.</span> The word \"oath\" shall be construed to include an affirmation in all cases in which,\n               by law, an affirmation may be substituted for an oath.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (k)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Officers, boards, etc.</span> Whenever reference is made to a particular officer, department, board, commission\n               or other agency, such reference shall be construed as if followed by the words \"of\n               the City of Norfolk, Virginia.\"\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               Any reference to any specific officer shall be deemed to include his duly authorized\n               deputy, agent or representative.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (l)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Person.</span> The word \"person\" may extend and be applied to associations, firms, partnerships\n               and bodies politic and corporate as well as to individuals.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (m)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Preceding, following.</span> The words \"preceding\" and \"following\" mean next before and next after, respectively.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (n)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">State or Commonwealth.</span> The word \"state\" or \"commonwealth\" shall be construed as if the words \"of Virginia\"\n               followed it.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (o)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">State Code.</span> References to the \"State Code\" or \"Code of Virginia\" shall mean the Code of Virginia,\n               1950, as amended.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (p)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Street.</span> The word \"street\" shall include streets, avenues, boulevards, highways, roads, alleys,\n               lanes, viaducts, bridges and the approaches thereto and all other public thoroughfares\n               in the city, and shall mean the entire width thereof between abutting property lines.\n               It shall be construed to include a sidewalk or footpath.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (q)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Swear; sworn.</span> The words \"swear\" and \"sworn\" shall be equivalent to the words \"affirm\" and \"affirmed\"\n               in all cases in which, by law, an affirmation may be substituted for an oath.\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"incr0\">\n               (r)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"content1\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Written; in writing.</span> The words \"written\" or \"in writing\" shall be construed to include any representation\n               of words, letters or figures, whether by printing or otherwise. (Code 1958, <a href=\"\" data-chunk-id=\"COCI_CH1GEPR_S1-2RUCODE\" class=\"section-link\" data-product-id=\"10121\">§ 1-2</a>)\n               </p>\n            \t\t\n            <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n               Similar definitions and rules of construction applicable to state law, Code of Virginia,\n               § 1-13.3 et seq.\n               </p></div>","SortDate":null,"Footnotes":null}],"NewOrds":[],"PdfUrl":null,"LastOrd":null,"PrevNode":{"Id":"COCI_CH1GEPR_S1-1HOCODECI","Heading":"Sec. 1-1. - How Code designated and cited.","NodeDepth":2,"HasChildren":false,"ParentId":"COCI_CH1GEPR","DocOrderId":209,"Children":[],"Data":{"NodeKey":null,"IsUpdated":false,"IsAmended":false,"HasAmendedDescendant":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocType":1,"DepthOverride":null,"ChunkGroupStartingId":null}},"NextNode":{"Id":"COCI_CH1GEPR_S1-3CASE","Heading":"Sec. 1-3. - Catchlines of sections.","NodeDepth":2,"HasChildren":false,"ParentId":"COCI_CH1GEPR","DocOrderId":211,"Children":[],"Data":{"NodeKey":null,"IsUpdated":false,"IsAmended":false,"HasAmendedDescendant":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocType":1,"DepthOverride":null,"ChunkGroupStartingId":null}},"ShowToc":false}